    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Soderstrom** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a strong 76.91 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against McGreevy is amplified by a +10% park factor and the premium slotting at #3 in the order, providing a rare convergence of high-volume opportunity and exploitable pitching. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier are **Brice Turang** (63.20) and **Josh Naylor** (62.00). **Brice Turang** continues to be a vital asset for our SB-starved build, and his projection is bolstered by an aggressive +8% adjustment for hitting second against Canning. **James Wood** (55.32) remains a high-upside play; despite a tougher matchup against Burns, the combination of a leadoff spot and a beneficial wind forecast makes him a critical component of our offensive engine.\n\nThe most challenging bench decision of the morning was keeping **Cole Young** on the sidelines. He flirted with the 40.0 threshold with a 39.51 score, but his presence in the bottom-third of the order against Burrows ultimately suppressed his upside too far to justify a start, especially with our strictly enforced daily efficiency floor. Conversely, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Seiya Suzuki** (47.22) and **Trevor Story** (45.72). Both are facing elite arms\u2014Sale and Luzardo, respectively\u2014where the SP skill penalties are significant. While we need their bats, we are monitoring these matchups closely; if **Trevor Story** struggles early against Luzardo\u2019s stuff, the risk of a sub-40 performance is non-trivial. With **Corbin Carroll** inactive today, we are leaning heavily on the platoon advantages of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and the park-adjusted output of **Henry Bolte** to maintain our momentum in the 5x5 standings.",
